       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg.\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is intended. If it is, I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it."
